    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n108186" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπογίγνομαι</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		 and later Gr. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπογεωργ-γίνομαι</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῑ</span>], <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>grow up after</i> or <i>in succession,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπαὶ δέ τε κόμπος ὀδόντων γίγνεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					11.417
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵνα σφι γενεὴ ὑπογίνηται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					3.159
				</span></i>
			; of inflammation following a hurt, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Art.</u>
				38
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ti.Locr.
				104a
			</span></i>; of feelings and thoughts, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				2.44.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				6.6.7
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
